# ============================================================================
#  .gitignore
#
#  Two categories here, and the comment on the second one matters:
#
#  1. Ordinary build output. Nothing generated should be committed.
#
#  2. Build output that lives INSIDE the source tree. res/Ribbon.bml is produced
#     by UICC from src/ribbon/Ribbon.xml, and rc.exe can only find it in the
#     directory of the .rc that references it -- there is no search path for
#     binary resource payloads. So it is written into res/ and must be ignored.
#     It is regenerated on every build; committing it would mean committing a
#     compiled artifact that silently goes stale.
#
#  A note on what is deliberately NOT ignored: nothing else is produced in the
#  source tree. If a new generated file appears in res/ or src/, add it here
#  rather than letting it get committed as if it were authored.
# ============================================================================

# -- build directories -------------------------------------------------------
build/
build32/
build64/
out/
cmake-build-*/
.vs/
*.vcxproj
*.vcxproj.*
*.sln
*.suo
*.user

# -- compiler and linker output ----------------------------------------------
*.obj
*.o
*.ilk
*.pdb
*.idb
*.exp
*.lib
*.dll
*.exe
*.exe.manifest.bak
*.res

# -- generated ribbon artifacts ----------------------------------------------
# See the header comment: generated in-tree by design, never committed.
res/Ribbon.bml
src/ribbon/RibbonIDs_gen.h

# -- editor and OS cruft ------------------------------------------------------
*.orig
*.rej
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# -- scratch ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anything a contributor dropped in for a one-off experiment.
scratch/
tmp/
